her  supposedly said pretty much trying to  start as much trouble as possible  one day natok found these insults to be  so offensive that he vowed he would kill  the eagle and in his anger he shook the  foundations of the tree so hard that the  entirety of the nine worlds trembled the  shaking of Yggdrasil and nidhogg being  set free from its roots are what many  considered to be two of the many signs  of ragnarok for those of you wanting to  know whether nidhogg was a serpent or a  dragon it's depicted as both and it's  commonplace in many cultures to see  dragons and serpents depicted as very  similar if not the same if you have any  thoughts or opinions that you'd like to  share then feel free to do so in the  comments below if you have enjoyed this  video then please consider leaving a  thumbs up as it really does help me and  the channel as always I've been your  host mythology in fiction explained  [Music]  you  [Music]  [Music]
 

